 ## Background
 The method is described in the context of digital geometry, specifically in the analysis of local methods for estimating surface properties of digitized solids [S1, book]. The analysis of its accuracy, particularly the lack of multigrid convergence and orientation-dependent errors, is detailed in works on 3D arc length, surface area, and curvature estimation [S1, book].
